From c9a0523541fc1035302d8f7c8f6f0509bfd87a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arthur Clark <mydevstuff@mail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:45:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] QNX: extend the LOK render gate to cover Draw and
 Impress

Add draw.fodg and impress.fodp fixtures (flat ODF, derived from the sd qa
data) and two gate cases that paint a whole-page 256x256 tile. The gate
now checks Writer + Calc + Math + Draw + Impress against per-document
non-white bands, with bad.odt as the negative control. This is both the
no-regression proof for the first three and the render proof that the sd
libraries load under the system-NSS build.

Change-Id: I7e5d6b9b31e152c15999ca0910919923947223e8
---
 libreofficekit/qa/qnxrendergate/README        |  4 +-
 .../qa/qnxrendergate/data/draw.fodg           | 56 +++++++++++++++
 .../qa/qnxrendergate/data/impress.fodp        | 70 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../qa/qnxrendergate/rendergate.cxx           |  7 +-
 4 files changed, 134 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libreofficekit/qa/qnxrendergate/data/draw.fodg
 create mode 100644 libreofficekit/qa/qnxrendergate/data/impress.fodp

diff --git a/libreofficekit/qa/qnxrendergate/README b/libreofficekit/qa/qnxrendergate/README
index 60bfefb30..f71e8e227 100644
--- a/libreofficekit/qa/qnxrendergate/README
+++ b/libreofficekit/qa/qnxrendergate/README
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@ Renders a 256x256 tile of each data/ document through LibreOfficeKit and checks
 the non-white pixel count against a per-document band: the floor rejects a blank
 tile, the ceiling rejects a garbage one. data/bad.odt is a negative control that
 must fail to render. Covers Writer (hello.docx, clean.odt) and Calc (calc.fods,
-flat ODF; painted over a fixed top-left twip region so the cells fill the tile), and Math (math.fodf, a flat ODF formula).
+flat ODF; painted over a fixed top-left twip region so the cells fill the tile),
+Math (math.fodf, a flat ODF formula), and Draw/Impress (draw.fodg, impress.fodp;
+flat ODF, whole-page tile).
 Substitutes the upstream tiledrendering/smoketest tests, which are unusable here
 (disabled/bit-rotted, and a whole-office build).
